@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #fafafa
skinparam node {
  BorderColor #c62828
  BackgroundColor #ffebee
}
skinparam cloud {
  BackgroundColor #e8f5e9
}

title Flujo Orquestador Real (EC2 + QEMU)\n3 tests · contra 34.193.139.170

node "Orquestador\nEC2 34.193.139.170\nUbuntu admin/linkguard123!" as EC2
node "QEMU orq\n192.168.100.10\nhost-lab" as ORQ_VM
node "QEMU pa\n192.168.100.20\nhost-lab" as PA_VM
node "QEMU pb\n192.168.100.30\nhost-lab" as PB_VM

cloud "Internet / AWS SG" as NET
cloud "br0/br1/br2\nred local QEMU" as BR

EC2 -down- NET
NET -down- BR
ORQ_VM -up- BR
PA_VM -up- BR
PB_VM -up- BR

note over EC2 : orch-cli --admin-token ...\nport 8000/RPC2\nWG Hub: 10.20.30.1

== test_register_qemu_peers ==
PA_VM -> EC2 : register_peer(qemu-pa, pubkey, user_id=qemu-pa)
PB_VM -> EC2 : register_peer(qemu-pb, pubkey, user_id=qemu-pb)
ORQ_VM -> EC2 : register_peer(qemu-orq, pubkey, user_id=qemu-orq)
EC2 --> ORQ_VM : {tunnel_ip: 10.20.30.7}
EC2 --> PA_VM : {tunnel_ip: 10.20.30.9}
EC2 --> PB_VM : {tunnel_ip: 10.20.30.10}
note over EC2 : wg show default → 3 peers visibles\nwg show default endpoints → IPs correctas
note over EC2 : orch-cli list-peers --network default\n→ peer01 peer02 peer03
note over ORQ_VM : user_id=qemu-orq (tenant)
note over PA_VM, PB_VM : user_id=qemu-pa, qemu-pb

== test_handshake_qemu_peers ==
PA_VM ->> EC2 : handshake iniciado (wg-quick up)
PB_VM ->> EC2 : handshake iniciado
ORQ_VM ->> EC2 : handshake iniciado
note over EC2 : wait 10s tras handshakes
EC2 -> EC2 : wg show default latest-handshakes\n→ todos los peers > 0 (reciente)

== test_ping_between_qemu_peers ==
PA_VM -> EC2 : ping -I wg0 10.20.30.10
EC2 -> PB_VM : reenvía (hub-spoke)
PB_VM --> EC2 : pong
EC2 --> PA_VM : pong
note over PA_VM : ping a 10.20.30.10 (pb) exitoso

PA_VM -> EC2 : ping -I wg0 10.20.30.7
EC2 --> PA_VM : pong
note over PA_VM : ping a 10.20.30.7 (orq) exitoso

PB_VM -> EC2 : ping -I wg0 10.20.30.9
EC2 -> PA_VM : reenvía
PA_VM --> EC2 : pong
EC2 --> PB_VM : pong

@enduml
